      "label": "1. Opening — India Through Time",
      "beats": [
        "Namaste, my little friend! Welcome to a very special story-time. Today, I am going to tell you a true story — the story of how our land got its many names. The chapter you are about to read carries a curious title: 'India, That Is Bharat'. Two names, one land. Are you ready? Let's sit down and listen…",
        "Look at this beautiful carving. It is roughly 2,300 years old, from the north gate of the Great Sanchi Stupa. People just like us — farmers, merchants, mothers, children — lived under the sky of this very land we now call India. They laughed, they played, they worked — just like you and me.",
        "The great philosopher Sri Aurobindo once wrote that 'the spiritual and cultural unity was made complete' in India 'between the Himalayas and the two seas'. Hold that image in your mind — tall mountains in the north, vast seas to the east and west. That is our land.",
        "Today, India is a modern nation — defined borders, defined states, a known population of more than a billion people. Maps are crisp, passports are stamped. But it was not always like this.",
        "Travel back 500 years. Travel back 2,000 years. Travel back 5,000 years. The borders shift, the names change, the kingdoms come and go. The land endures; its identity evolves — like a river that keeps flowing, even as its banks change.",
        "This region of the world — which we today call the 'Indian Subcontinent' — has been called by many names. Some were given by her own inhabitants. Some were given by visitors from Persia, Greece, China, and beyond. Each name is like a piece of a great mosaic.",
        "And here are the two big questions we will answer in this story: First — how do we define India? Second — what were the ancient names for India? In our next story, we will look at the land itself. Ready? Let's turn the page…"
      ],
